# Anti-Patterns

## Architecture Violations
- **Never import `@repo/core` from `@repo/shared`** — shared is a leaf package with zero internal deps
- **Never put I/O in `@repo/core`** — engine is pure logic; all I/O goes through `PersistenceAdapter`
- **Never call `/api/*` routes from the web app** — web is read-only and must use `/public/*` only
- **Never bypass `enforcePolicy()`** — all role-gated actions must check policy before executing
- **Never skip status transition validation** — use `isValidTransition()` from `@repo/shared/statuses`

## Data Handling
- **Never store raw JSON objects in SQLite** — Prisma stores JSON as strings; always serialize/deserialize via adapter helpers
- **Never hardcode `OPENAI_API_KEY`** or any secret — read from environment variables
- **Never log event payloads containing secrets** — events are persisted to SQLite and broadcast via WebSocket
- **Never mutate canonical artifacts directly** — only `GRAIN_ELEVATOR` role (via merge) can modify canonical

## Code Style
- **Never use CommonJS** (`require`/`module.exports`) — all packages are ESM (`"type": "module"`)
- **Never define prop types in separate `types` files** — use inline object types on components
- **Never use `.prettierrc`** — project uses Prettier defaults only
- **Never create non-flat ESLint configs** — all configs must be flat format (`eslint.config.mjs`)
- **Never omit `"use client"` on shared UI components** — all `@repo/ui` components need the directive

## Testing
- **Never depend on SQLite in unit tests** — use `InMemoryAdapter` from `@repo/core/src/testing/`
- **Never skip Zod validation on API boundaries** — all request/response payloads are schema-validated

## Agent Management
- **Never spawn agents without a role assignment** — every `AgentSession` requires a `roleId`
- **Never skip worktree cleanup** — call `WorktreeManager.remove()` when sessions end
